ased estimate.", "watch": "Any independent or high-quality polling confirming the Democratic-sponsored surveys' tied picture would make this a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Blake Moore (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Blake Moore, the Republican incumbent, enters the general election after surviving a contested primary against Karianne Lisonbee in Utah's redrawn second district. The seat leans Republican by about fifteen points, and Moore holds an overwhelming financial edge, with roughly $1.9 million on hand compared to about $23,000 for Democrat Peter Crosby, who has raised little and drawn no outside spending.\n\nThe main wrinkle is polling: two surveys commissioned by Crosby's own campaign show the race essentially tied, and local coverage has echoed that framing. However, partisan-sponsored polls deserve caution, and prediction markets still give Moore about a 94% chance of winning. The forecast expects Moore to prevail by a comfortable but not overwhelming margin, with meaningful uncertainty given the conflicting signals.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0478, "margin": -11.61}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0598, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0822, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0948, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0534, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.112, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2129, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1726, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1389, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1163, "margin": -8.0}]}